;; WAIVERS for the structural Clojure gates — one key per check.
;;
;; AN EXEMPTION IS A WAIVER FOR A TRUE FALSE POSITIVE, never a disabled rule, and
;; the four mandatory fields are what separate the two:
;;
;;   :rationale     why this specific case is NOT a defect
;;   :retires-when  the EVENT that makes the entry unnecessary — no date can
;;                  express a condition, which is why this survives :expires
;;   :owner         who to ask. The check is `non-blank string`, so this buys a
;;                  name to route the expiry failure to, never verification
;;   :expires       ISO-8601, at most 90 days out. Expiry and horizon are separate
;;                  hard failures so neither masks the other
;;
;; A STALE ENTRY — one matching no live finding — IS ITSELF A HARD FAILURE. That is
;; the down-only half of the ratchet: without it an entry outlives the finding it
;; excused, silently widening the unchecked surface, and an offender can be fixed
;; while its excuse stays behind. So deleting a waiver is part of fixing the thing
;; it waived.
;;
;; The key set is CLOSED. A typo is refused rather than silently widening what the
;; entry swallows.
;;
;; MATCHING IS :file AND :name TOGETHER. Either alone would turn one entry into a
;; whole-file skip, or into a licence for a same-named var anywhere in the tree.
;;
;; EMPTY IS THE INTENDED STATE. Both checks are green with no waivers at all; an
;; entry here is a claim that a check is WRONG about one specific case, and it must
;; argue that rather than assert it.
{:docstrings []
 ;; spec-presence is seeded so it is green with NO waivers, which is what makes
 ;; the enrolment a scope declaration rather than a guess: a scope that still
 ;; needed waivers on arrival would not have been measured, only hoped at.
 :spec-presence []
 :spec-shape [{:file "tools/renderer-gen/src/lvgl_codegen/normalize.clj"
               :name "proto3-default?"
               :rationale "strip-defaults calls this predicate on each MAP VALUE it encounters at any depth of its recursion (normalize.clj's remove step), and a map value may be nil, a numeric/string/boolean scalar default, an enum-zero keyword or an empty or non-empty collection. proto_ser_boundary_test exercises these branches through the instrumented vars; a map-only input would reject legitimate calls. Renewal reviewed against that actual caller; this entry excuses only the predicate's heterogeneous argument."
               :retires-when "The normalized IR becomes a closed recursive value domain shared by strip-defaults and this predicate, allowing a truthful named argument schema instead of arbitrary values."
               :owner "gate-port"
               :expires "2026-11-02"}
              {:file "tools/renderer-gen/src/lvgl_codegen/normalize.clj"
               :name "strip-defaults"
               :rationale "The function recurses through its own instrumented var on every map value and vector element, then returns scalar leaves unchanged. proto_ser_boundary_test directly exercises nil/scalars, nested maps and vectors and protobuf canonicalization. Both argument and return therefore remain heterogeneous at the recursive var boundary. Renewal reviewed against the actual recursion; unlike scan-ambiguous-keys, recursion does re-enter this public var."
               :retires-when "The normalized IR gains a closed recursive value schema covering every caller and leaf, or the recursive helper is separated from a narrower public IR boundary."
               :owner "gate-port"
               :expires "2026-11-02"}]}
